                        "content": "The nurse is assisting in the care of a client who is being evaluated for possible myasthenia gravis. The primary health care provider gives a test dose of edrophonium. Evaluation of the results indicates that the test is positive. Which would be the expected response noted by the nurse?",
                        "subjectId": "ad5ab04c79144c0ea9b83385308c3b1d",
                        "difficultyIds": "a0f7d178f7b728b8bba7ef20ddeca62d",
                        "difficulty": "考试范围-Evaluating 评价",
                        "textAnalysis": "Rationale:\nEdrophonium is a short-acting acetylcholinesterase inhibitor used to diagnose myasthenia gravis. An increase in muscle strength would be seen in 1 to 3 minutes following the test dose if the client does have the disease. If no response occurs, another dose is given over the next 2 minutes and muscle strength is tested again. If no increase in muscle strength occurs with this higher dose, the muscle weakness is not caused by myasthenia gravis. Clients who receive injections of this medication commonly demonstrate a drop in blood pressure, feel faint and dizzy, and are flushed.",
                        "id": "0fc70b418e4747b1965ea469950fa9c9",
                        "mark": "0",
                        "collectionState": "0"
                    },
                    {
                        "optionList": [
                            {
                                "isRight": "1",
                                "userAnswer": "",
                                "isSelected": "0",
                                "id": "2d971a624ec0495ca2b3dea7f469544b",
                                "content": "Intake and output"
                            },
                            {
                                "isRight": "0",
                                "userAnswer": "",
                                "isSelected": "0",
                                "id": "600cb015d9c44a8a811c5f5dce8470de",
                                "content": "The prothrombin time"
                            },
                            {
                                "isRight": "0",
                                "userAnswer": "",
                                "isSelected": "0",
                                "id": "488810d4791947ba8342a5c190609dc8",
                                "content": "The pupillary response"
                            },
                            {
                                "isRight": "0",
                                "userAnswer": "",
                                "isSelected": "0",
                                "id": "5d3f7bc2ade44f579c0e1fa73504b7c4",
                                "content": "The partial thromboplastin time"
                            }
                        ],
                        "extJson": {
                            "optionList": [
                                {
                                    "isRight": "1",
                                    "userAnswer": "",
                                    "isSelected": "0",
                                    "id": "2d971a624ec0495ca2b3dea7f469544b",
                                    "content": "Intake and output"
                                },
                                {
                                    "isRight": "0",
                                    "userAnswer": "",
                                    "isSelected": "0",
                                    "id": "600cb015d9c44a8a811c5f5dce8470de",
                                    "content": "The prothrombin time"
                                },
                                {
                                    "isRight": "0",
                                    "userAnswer": "",
                                    "isSelected": "0",
                                    "id": "488810d4791947ba8342a5c190609dc8",
                                    "content": "The pupillary response"
                                },
                                {
                                    "isRight": "0",
                                    "userAnswer": "",
                                    "isSelected": "0",
                                    "id": "5d3f7bc2ade44f579c0e1fa73504b7c4",
                                    "content": "The partial thromboplastin time"
