                        "difficultyIds": "80db17ea97ed8fdcd1b6b9666390fca1",
                        "difficulty": "考试范围-Applying 应用",
                        "textAnalysis": "Rationale:\nCarbamazepine is classified as an iminostilbene derivative and is used as an anticonvulsant, antineuralgic, antimanic, and antipsychotic. The medication can cause blood dyscrasias as an adverse effect, and the client would have a CBC count done before therapy and periodically during therapy. Additional laboratory tests that need to be done include a serum iron determination, urinalysis, blood urea nitrogen determination, and carbamazepine level. The tests identified in the remaining options are unnecessary.",
